{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample","id":1393164,"title":"Catalog: Mannikins (2nd Sample)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-31T11:45:31-07:00","id":1393164,"title":"Catalog: Mannikins (2nd Sample)","content":"A second sample of my lost Project, &quot;Catalog: Mannikins&quot;<br /> <br /> 5<sup>th</sup> floor: The Unblinking People.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b><br /> Follow the steps in \u201cInanimae: the Secret Way\u201d.<br /> <b>Step One: Character Concept.</b><br /> Choose concept, Court, Legacy, Jeu, Style and Salon (optional)<br /> <b>Step Two: Select Attributes.</b><br /> <i>Prioritize</i> the three categories: Physical, Social and Mental (7/5/3)<br /> Or<br /> <i>Divide</i> 15 points between the nine Attributes.<br /> Mannikins begin with 1 point in each attribute, like all other characters.<br /> <b>Step Three: Select Abilities.</b><br /> <i>Divide</i> 27 points between all the Abilities you posses.<br /> Mannikins do not usually prioritize their Ability Categories (check with your Storyteller this step!).<br /> <b>Step Four: Select Advantages.</b><br /> <i>Choose</i> Backgrounds (5) and Realms (5). Mannikins may choose both Inanimae Realms and Kithain Ones, but they rarely mix both of them.<br /> <i>Choose</i> Slivers and/or Arts (as determined by your Jeu)<br /> <b>Step Five: Finishing Touches.</b><br /> <i>Record</i> beginning Glamour, Willpower and Banality as determined by your Jeu (check Inanimae: the Secret Way)<br /> <i>Record</i> Birthrights and Frailties, and Style\u2019s Boon and Flaw.<br /> <i>Spend</i> freebie points (15)<br /> <i>Choose</i> Merits and Flaws.<br /> <br /> <b>Mannikins\u2019 Birthrights and Frailties (Obsolete)</b><br /> The mannikins\u2019 Birthrights and Frailties were dropped from \u201cInanimae: the Secret Way\u201d and appeared in MET format in the \u201c<b>Shining Host Player\u2019s Guide</b>\u201d. This tabletop version includes the Styles, and is the one I use in my <b>Changeling</b> campaigns.<br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights</b>:<ul><li><b>Human Touch</b>: Forged from ideals of human perfection, all mannikins get<br /> three free dots in the Husk Background. Mannikins of the Jouet Style gain an additional Charisma point. Mannikins of all other Styles gain an additional Appearance point.</li> <li><b>Jack-of-All-Trades</b>: Can learn Kithain Arts and Realms, and may learn Inanimae Slivers and Realms. They may also take any Backgrounds, including those normally reserved for other Inanimae.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Frailties</b>:<ul><li><b>Master of None:</b> Cannot master any Art or Sliver (they cannot attain level 5). Also, mannikins do not posses an Affinity.</li> <li><b>Spark of Life</b>: While they are a good imitation of human life, there is always something odd or alien about a mannikin appearance. They get a +1 difficulty in all Social rolls against mortals who know their true nature, even if they have managed to get their trust (i.e. Allies). Most mannikins are quite sensitive about this flaw, and will become resentful of those who insist on reminding them of it.</li> <li><b>Velveteen Dreams</b>: All mannikins are interested in the Heart Riddle, and all would love to become \u201creal\u201d humans. They must make a Willpower roll to avoid exploring any possibility or chance to become real when presented with one, no matter how remote.</li> </ul><b>Styles &amp; Salons</b><br /><br /> Styles are both like and unlike the Sidhe Houses; all mannikins belong to one, but the choice is irreversible. You can only change your Style if you adopt a new Anchor, and that is something that most mannikins would prefer not to think about, ever. Nevertheless, they are also unlike the Houses; Styles are not fraternities, families or secret societies\u2026 they are more like \u201coutlooks\u201d or \u201clifestyles\u201d. Mannikins bound to similar Anchors usually possess similar outlooks, tastes, preferences\u2026 and they tend to stick together. Salons, on the other hand, are like political impulses, or private clubs. A mannikin does not have to belong to a Salon, but all mannikins belong to a Style.<br /> If an Anchor is destroyed, mannikins usually bind themselves to a new one from the same Style. (You should read more about this in Inanimae: the Secret Way, pg. 75)<br /> <br /> If a mannikin changes his Style, he will enter a dazzling world of changing-alliances and mixed reactions from both the members of his new Style and his former friends. If the Anchor of a Natural is Krofted, of course, the Natural becomes a Krofted mannikin (most likely a Top Model, a Supplicant or a Phidian), and he is sure to find himself surrounded by new faces.<br /> <br /> All Styles posses a cost in Freebie points, reflecting their relative rarity in the modern world. Finally, all members of a Style receive both a Boon and a Ban.<br /> <br /> While it is unusual for mannikins to change their Salon\u2019s affiliation, it can and does happen. Mannikins of the Automata Style are highly vocal about their membership in a given Craft or Factory Salon, and anyone hosting a meeting of Automata mannikins is careful not to invite members of opposed Salons, unless a verbal (and sometimes physical) confrontation is the desired goal.<br /> Most Supplicants are ideologically, if not formally, members of a Craft Salon. On the other hand, most Top Models agree with the Factory theories, but there are still some Fashion Victims allied with the Craft Salons. There are more Factory Toys than Craft Toys, but as members of this Style tend to be gentle and the Style itself lacks the venomous internal-politics that plague others, the Craft-Factory conflict is seen as a quite boring and banal matter.<br /> The Manzolini mannikins aligned with the Craft Salons form a kind of gerontocracy, but one that is willing to listen to the arguments of the Factory thinkers; all in all, argue the Manzolini, all human beings are quite similar to each other if you stop to look under their skin, so why should mannikins not follow their lead? Naturals, being Gladeling mannikins, are outside the bounds of the Craft/Factory debate, and form something of a \u201cSalon without members\u201d. If hot-tempered debates arise, Naturals tend to align with the Free-thought Salons. Finally, Statues affirm that their style does not posses any Factory members, and that the concept itself is ludicrous, so nobody has yet heard about a Phidian being member of a Factory Salon.<br /> <br /> <b>Salons:</b><br /> It is important to remember that Salons are much more important in the Dreaming than in Earth (specially when you are in Capecia!). Mannikins dominate the Empire of Dolls because they are both smarter and more numerous than all the other chimerical doll races together, but there are many, many members of the Salons that are not mannikins. For instance, there are many bronze talking heads, like those built by Greeks and Romans, belonging to the Copelli Salon. They are not mannikins, because they lack a human-like body.<br /> <br /> <b>- \u010capek:</b><br /> The members of this Salon, called Bots, are spread along a spectrum of Factory ideologies, from the hard-core radicals of the Removers of Identity to the moderates of the League for a Better Tomorrow. The Mechs dominate numerically the \u010capek Salon; its Top Model members write many of its ideological treatises and propaganda.<br /> Members of this Salon advocate the homogeneity of Husks as the most desirable quality of mannikins, and reason that differences between individual Husks are the seeds of social unrest and disorder. Young Kithain tend to call Bots \u201cfascists\u201d, but this term is meaningless for the Inanimae; those of the mannikins who have studied the history of the Autumn World are quick to pinpoint ideological differences between the \u010capek Salon and the Italian and German Fascist Parties of the 30\u2019s.<br /> The radical thinkers and academics of this Salon, on the other hand, tend to dismiss these critics with the all-too-often-heard phrase (first heard in the Capecia Senate, addressed by a \u010capek Senator to a Sidhe Ambassador, or so it is said): \u201cYou meat won\u2019t understand\u201d.<br /> There are other Factory Salons, mainly the radical Cyberdreams Salon (sponsored by some filthy rich citizens of the Cybernetic Quarter of Capecia). The Cyberdreams Salon advocates the destruction of all non-homogenous Husks and the proclamation of a decree forbidding the creation of such Husks. Their presence in the Capecian Senate is purely symbolic. The long, tedious speeches of the Senators of the Cyberdreams Salon are usually embarrassing for the Bots, because even the hard-core advocates of Factory know that it is technically impossible to craft 100% identical Husks without losing them to Banality.<ul><li><b>Copelli:</b></li> </ul>The Copelli Salon did not exist before the implement of mass-production by Henry Ford in the beginning of the XX century. Previously, Craft had been the dominant movement in the theoretical and philosophical landscape of Capecia, and advocates of Factory had been rare. Many \u201cguilds\u201d and \u201ccraft schools\u201d existed that defended the creation of Husks and the superiority of hand-made Anchors, but there was not a common line of thought, a theoretical fundament or a manifest. All of this became a need after the founding of the \u010capek Salon.<br /> Members of the Copelli Salon, like their counterparts in the \u010capek Salon, are spread along the whole spectrum of Craft philosophy: from the moderates of Manufactures of Glamour Inc. to the hard-line radicals of the Thousand Toy-Makers.<br /> To the Copelli, as each faerie spirit is an individual, each Husk should be different from all others. They see mass-produced Husks and Anchors as abominations, or at least as poor substitutes for the hand-made, traditional ones. They point to the dangers of Quickmadness, the variety of Bedlam that affects mannikins of the Factory Salons. Moreover, they look at the impersonal look of the Factory Husk, and label it \u201cugly\u201d.<br /> To Bots (and many Kithain), the Copelli are elitists and sickly refined in their tastes and mannerisms. Their mechanical movements (the Copelli Salon is numerically dominated by the Alberti and the Manzolini) are frightening and creepy in their beauty.<br /> There are other Craft Salons, but their membership is low, and their participation in the Senate is minimal. The most radical of these is the Luddite Salon: some of these Inanimae are so set in their hatred for the Factory that have resorted to terrorist acts, such as the use of Engine Poison against Mechs and Factory Manzolini, and the use of explosives in the corridors of Capecia controlled by the Factory Salons.<ul><li><b>Rotwang:</b></li> </ul>No single Style dominates the Rotwang Salon. There are as many Top Models as Supplicants in this menagerie of \u201cliberal\u201d, \u201cdemocratic\u201d, \u201canarchistic\u201d mannikins. If only, there is a slight majority of Statues, but that is probably due to the fact that Statues resent any political impulse not led by themselves, and that many of them love to talk endlessly about the glorious, bygone days of the Greeks and the Romans.<br /> Rotwang philosophy treads a middle ground between Copellian idealism and the stultifying pragmatism of the \u010capek Salon. Members of this Salon recognize the individuality of a given mannikin, and support the right to posses a hand-made body. However, they doubt the desirability of the mass-produced Husks recommended by the hard-core members of the Factory Salons.<br /> Moreover, members of the Rotwang Salon support the right of individual mannikins to use Factory-produced Husks, unlike the more orthodox members of the Copelli Salon.<br /> Rotwang are not very strong currently at the Capecian Senate, but they are slowly increasing their numbers as the two varieties of Bedlam that affect the Inanimae, Dumbmadness and Quickmadness, are claiming the minds of more and more citizens of Capecia. In addition, they are progressively gaining the support of the few Naturals who are members of the Senate. Soon, they could ally with the more liberal members of the Copelli and force the abdication of the High Dux.<br /> There are no other significant Free-Thought Salons. There is, however, a terrorist group (\u201cCog Boyz\u201d) formed by a renegade, splinter bunch of Mechs that grew disfranchised with the cautious, moderate policy of the Rotwang Salon. These \u201cCog Boyz\u201d claim the Senate is an outdated institution, and that what Capecia needs is a consensual, anarchistic government. Passersby have spotted Members of this group fighting both the Luddite Salon and the Capecian Ducal Guard.<br /> <br /> <b>Styles:</b><ul><li><b>Automata (freebie cost: 1)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Alberti (Craft) / Mechs (Factory)</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Automata mannikins are expert crafters and artisans. They gain a free dot in the Crafts Skill (usually Clockwork or Electronics), and cannot botch Crafts rolls.</li> <li><b>Ban: </b>Members of this Style tend to be cold and detached. Their Empathy Talent cannot be higher than half their Glamour score (rounding up); this Style is deeply split between Craft and Factory, and Automata members of a Salon suffer a +1 difficulty in all Social rolls against Automata members of an opposed Salon.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Ceremonial (freebie cost: 2)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Supplicants &amp; Sepulchrals</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Ceremonial mannikins are solemn and formal. They gain a free dot in the Etiquette Skill, and cannot botch Etiquette rolls. All Ceremonials posses 1 free dot in the Relevance Background.</li> <li><b>Ban:</b> Stone Supplicants are disliked by Glomes, and Wood Supplicants are disliked by Kuberas; both phyla see them as agents of the Krofted, and they suffer a +1 difficulty penalty to all their Social rolls against members of the pertinent Phylum. Supplicants whose Anchors are made not of stone or wood suffer this penalty with both Kuberas and Glomes (they think they are cover-agents).</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Fashion (freebie cost: 0)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Top Models &amp; Fashion Victims</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Fashion mannikins are the most common, and the most used to deal with humans. They begin the game with a free dot in the Empathy talent, and posses a \u20131 difficulty to all Empathy rolls.</li> <li><b>Ban:</b> Most mortals (and some supernaturals) tend to feel betrayed after discovering that the Top Models are not \u201calive\u201d. Fashion mannikins suffer a +2 difficulty to all Social rolls (instead of the usual +1) with people who know their true nature, unless they manage to gain their trust again.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Jouet (freebie cost: 0)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Toys &amp; Game Partners</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Toys are always willing to play with children, and are used to their ways and manners. Toys gain a free dot in the Empathy talent and posses a \u20132 difficulty to all Empathy rolls with children only.</li> <li><b>Ban:</b> Toys must buy the Flaw: Small, but receive no free points for it. Their Husks always look like children (when weeks pass, they look like wizened, gnarled children!), and their Dream forms are always small. Moreover, they are not taken seriously by other mannikins, and cannot posses more than 3 points in the Relevance Background.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Manzolini (freebie cost: 2)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Plastic Corpses &amp; Waxworks</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Waxworks are experts in the activities that surround their Anchors: Anatomy and Medicine. They gain a free dot in the Medicine or Science (Anatomy) Knowledge, and cannot botch Medicine rolls. All Manzolini Husks possess internal organs; due to this fact, Manzolini gain an additional dot in the Husk Background (up to a maximum of 5).</li> <li><b>Ban:</b> Manzolini are creepy. Mortals and other un-enchanted beings tend to feel uncomfortable around these mannikins, and they suffer a +1 difficulty on most Social rolls (except Intimidation). When building a Husk, Manzolini cannot help creating removable skin-plaques; if these are retired, the veins, arteries, tendons, intestines, etc\u2026 are fully visible, and the Manzolini\u2019s Appearance drops to 0 (however, Manzolini without their skin-plaques gain a \u20132 difficulty to their Intimidation rolls)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Natural (freebie cost: 0)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Naturals</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Despite their instincts, Gladeling Inanimae trust Naturals. Naturals gain a free dot in the Survival talent, and posses a \u20131 difficulty to all Social rolls with Gladeling Inanimae.</li> <li><b>Ban:</b> Naturals are looked down by other mannikins, and suffer a +1 difficulty to all Social rolls with non-Natural mannikins.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Phidian (freebie cost: 2)</b><ul><li><b>Nickname:</b> Statues &amp; Golems.</li> <li><b>Boon:</b> Statues are sages and keepers of lore. They gain a free dot in Academics, Gremayre, Occult or Lore (Dreaming) Knowledge, and cannot botch rolls in their field of study (if the player chooses a free dot in Academics, the character cannot botch Academics rolls). Moreover, they are solid and stoic, and posses a free additional Bruised Health Level.</li> <li><b>Ban: </b> Statues are haughty and patronizing, and tend to disdain the comments of those they perceive as inferior to themselves. As a result, they suffer a +1 difficulty to all Social rolls (including Intimidation). They are also vulnerable to flattery, and suffer a +1 difficulty to all Empathy rolls while being flattered.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> New Background: <b>Relevance</b><br /> Mannikin society lacks the stiff, feudal rigidity of Kithain society, and possesses instead a more flexible social structure. The mannikins call this curious mix of modernism, personal qualities, castes and status \u201cRelevance\u201d, and it measures a given mannikin\u2019s importance and position in the society of the Unblinking People. It measures also the degree other mannikins have heard about the character.<br /> Mannikins, like all other Inanimae, cannot be affected by Sovereign, regardless their Relevance rating, unless they have accepted a formal title in Kithain society.<br /> Relevance correlates sometimes, not always, with Status (which measures the position of an Inanimae among all other Inanimae). (i.e. Black Robes (who must posses Status 5, tend also to posses Relevance 4-5). However, this is not obligatory, because you could be very famous among the Inanimae (high Status) but not very known among the mannikins (low Relevance).<br /> All Supplicants possess at least Relevance 1, reflecting their prestige and influence in mannikin society.<br /> x Nobody knows your face. You are a second-class citizen.<br /> \u25cf You are recognized as a citizen, but granted no special privileges: Toy worker, upcoming Top Model, unimportant Supplicant.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf You are a member of the low-middle class: successful novice Top Models, artisan Alberti and Mechs, Manzolini herbalists and apothecaries.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You are a successful middle-class citizen of the Empire of Dolls: Toy magistrates and senators, ambitious Top Models, looked-down Supplicants &amp; Statues.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You are one of the movers and shakers of Imperial policy: Natural &amp; Top Model senators, Manzolini anatomists, Alberti &amp; Mech Master Artisans.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf You are one of the most important citizens of the Empire, and you are respected everywhere: Supplicant, Manzolini, Alberti &amp; Mech senators, Salon Leader, Top Model couturier (yes!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T14:52:32-07:00","id":1393222,"title":"","content":"Yes! We need more Manikin stuff! I had so many questions and when I asked nobody answered, not even non canon homebrew style answers!<br /> <br /> I would snatch this up in a heartbeat!<br /> <br /> Edit: also I didn\u2019t know they had a cut birthrite!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  Edit 05-31-2020, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T15:30:01-07:00","id":1393236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393222#post1393222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! We need more Manikin stuff! I had so many questions and when I asked nobody answered, not even non canon homebrew style answers!<br /> <br /> I would snatch this up in a heartbeat!<br /> <br /> Edit: also I didn\u2019t know they had a cut birthrite!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a lot, Eldagusto.<br /> <br /> Say, have you got any specific comments, questions, likes or dislikes about this draft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:29:14-07:00","id":1393251,"title":"","content":"Styles is a good idea, I do feel there is a good amount of space that can be filled by making Manikins more then just one type. And it makes sense because now Fashion Manikins are different from clockwork men.<br /> <br /> And do you have any opinions on slivers and realms for Manikins. I plan to revise Slivers but I am still tossing around a lot of ideas for what I should do for Realms concerning inanimate.<br /> <br /> And how do you imagine the Empire of Dolls and the Empire of Flickers relate? I have plans for Flickers and Cinema Archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T21:28:38-07:00","id":1393337,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I will take a look at your thread on fixing Slivers.<br /> <br /> What about the glossary? I'm particularly proud of the Manzolini. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T02:54:14-07:00","id":1393380,"title":"","content":"I just noticed this was two threads, I was confused for a sec when I couldn't find things I knew I read before.<br /> <br /> But now that I fully read both pages its very fitting. Considering Mannikins were supposed to be a secretly populous group of Fae it really needed this fleshing out. And I feel Statues and such fit better here then with Glomes. Its less confusing to have human effigies be Mannikins and Stone constructs not in human form as Glomes. Do non human toys like Velveteen Rabbits live with the The Jouet in the Empire of Dolls? Do you plan to address things like other Inanimae Phyla waking up from Slumber having joined the Ranks of the Mannikins, like the Idea Pinocchio started as a log and was made into a Jouet. It really makes sense the Statues aren't mass Produced, and I really like the introduction of the divide between Massproduced and Custom Made Mannikins, it really makes sense since they are so heavily oriented towards Krofted, and the idea of their Unique forms of Bedlam is also intriguing, and I like the names.<br /> <br /> Manzolini provide a much needed shock of Horror as before the basic Fashion Mannikin was very much built off the eerie Uncanny Valley effect, and I can't believe I didn't think of Waxwork anatomical Mannikins they also share a similar disconcerting aura. Though I did think of Corpse Inanimae partially from the inspiration of the Human Anatomy Museum of Luigi Rolando when I initially was brainstorming the ideas for Osseus and Thanatos Slivers.<br /> <br /> Copelli, Capek and Rotwang are all literary references right?<br /> <br /> And Relevance also is something that seems fitting, after they initially said Inanimae don't have Title but they are all noble it left something to be desired.<br /> <br /> So one question do you think when Inanimae on Earth are Slumbering they are awake in their Home Empires? If they weren't it feels they would be a lot more empty unless they were almost entirely populated by Chimerical only Denizens.<br /> <br /> So far we only have rules for Inanimae already on the Autumn World waking up, but you introduce the idea of a lot of the Empires Populations existing only in the Dreaming, how do you imagine these type of beings being able to get Anchors, would it be during Resurgence like Events? Do you Imagine the Empire of Dolls and Empire of Flickers essentially exploded in size after the Technology to bring them into prominence rose in the last couple centuries? Like the ones without Anchors are both Those who abandoned the Mortal's World and those birthed by new inventions as well as science fiction and the like?<br /> <br /> This finally gives me something to grab onto besides the very nebulous concepts we had for how to handle Mannikins in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T03:09:30-07:00","id":1393382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed this was two threads, I was confused for a sec when I couldn't find things I knew I read before.<br /> Manzolini provide a much needed shock of Horror as before the basic Fashion Mannikin was very much built off the eerie Uncanny Valley effect, and I can't believe I didn't think of Waxwork anatomical Mannikins they also share a similar disconcerting aura. Though I did think of Corpse Inanimae partially from the inspiration of the Human Anatomy Museum of Luigi Rolando when I initially was brainstorming the ideas for Osseus and Thanatos Slivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manzolini as a term is my own creation, and a reference to two anatomists: Giovanni Manzolini and Anna Morandi, his wife.<br /> <br /> Most other terms are taken from the brief description of Capecia in &quot;Dreams and Nightmares&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will try to address all your other questions later; now I'm marking exams and should be working, LOL. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:41:10-07:00","id":1393466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just noticed this was two threads, I was confused for a sec when I couldn't find things I knew I read before.<br /> <br /> But now that I fully read both pages its very fitting. Considering Mannikins were supposed to be a secretly populous group of Fae it really needed this fleshing out. And I feel Statues and such fit better here then with Glomes.<br /> Its less confusing to have human effigies be Mannikins and Stone constructs not in human form as Glomes.<br /> Do non human toys like Velveteen Rabbits live with the The Jouet in the Empire of Dolls?<br /> Do you plan to address things like other Inanimae Phyla waking up from Slumber having joined the Ranks of the Mannikins, like the Idea Pinocchio started as a log and was made into a Jouet.</div> </div> </div> </div>- I think this wouldn't be something that would turn a Kubera into a Mannikin... such a radical transformation of an Anchor would change a Gladeling into a Krofted, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really makes sense the Statues aren't mass Produced, and I really like the introduction of the divide between Massproduced and Custom Made Mannikins, it really makes sense since they are so heavily oriented towards Krofted, and the idea of their Unique forms of Bedlam is also intriguing, and I like the names.</div> </div> </div> </div>These concepts are from &quot;Dreams and Nightmares&quot;, I didn't invent them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manzolini provide a much needed shock of Horror as before the basic Fashion Mannikin was very much built off the eerie Uncanny Valley effect, and I can't believe I didn't think of Waxwork anatomical Mannikins they also share a similar disconcerting aura. Though I did think of Corpse Inanimae partially from the inspiration of the Human Anatomy Museum of Luigi Rolando when I initially was brainstorming the ideas for Osseus and Thanatos Slivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are these Osseus and Thanatos Slivers...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copelli, Capek and Rotwang are all literary references right?</div> </div> </div> </div>This terms are from &quot;Dreams and Nightmares&quot;; Capek refers to Karol Capek, the writer who invented the word &quot;robot&quot; in his work &quot;RUR&quot;. Rotwang refers to the mad scientist in Fritz Lang's Metropolis. Copelli refers to a mechanical girl in Delibes' ballet, Copp\u00e9lia, inspired in turn by Hoffmann's story Der Sandman. Copelia seems to be derived from the Greek for 'young woman'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Relevance also is something that seems fitting, after they initially said Inanimae don't have Title but they are all noble it left something to be desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393164-catalog-mannikins-2nd-sample?p=1393380#post1393380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one question do you think when Inanimae on Earth are Slumbering they are awake in their Home Empires? If they weren't it feels they would be a lot more empty unless they were almost entirely populated by Chimerical only Denizens.<br /> <br /> So far we only have rules for Inanimae already on the Autumn World waking up, but you introduce the idea of a lot of the Empires Populations existing only in the Dreaming, how do you imagine these type of beings being able to get Anchors, would it be during Resurgence like Events? Do you Imagine the Empire of Dolls and Empire of Flickers essentially exploded in size after the Technology to bring them into prominence rose in the last couple centuries? Like the ones without Anchors are both Those who abandoned the Mortal's World and those birthed by new inventions as well as science fiction and the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... so many questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:14:17-07:00","id":1393515,"title":"","content":"I need to look back on dreams and nightmares.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well I figured the empire of dolls initially were probably populated by Krofted of all types who found more in common with each other through their effigy Anchors rather then their past association with their old empires. Cause things start to get confusing when you see a Mannikins anchor and you aren\u2019t sure if they are a Mannikin or a glome or solimander.<br /> <br /> Also a lot of the initial Inanimae write up had me question if Mannikins were the one Inanimae who turned their Anchors into their Husks. It would seem appropriate based on the inspirational material where the Mannikins literally come to life, rather then have human avatars. Hmm like I wonder what the home inside of a Mannikins anchor looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T20:10:32-07:00","id":1507543,"title":"","content":"I'm back in the Forums after a two-year-long depression. Sorry about the necroposting. Any comments on these, New Forumites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}